<title>INDIA: Indian silver ends unchanged, gold almost steady.</title>
<headline>Indian silver ends unchanged, gold almost steady.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold prices opened higher on the back of recovery in the world market but held steady at that level during on Thursday amid limited activity, dealer said.</p>
<p>Physical buying was limited and the sentiment was subdued at the end of the session, they said.</p>
<p>Gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) settled 100 rupees higher at 59,800 rupees per piece.</p>
<p>Silver opened higher but demand resistance capped early gains towards the close, dealers said.  </p>
